---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {sources, roots, titles} from '../lib/data';
import sourceIndex from '../../public/data/source_index.json';
const used=new Map<number,Set<string>>(Object.entries(sourceIndex).map(([i,government])=>[Number(i),new Set(government as string[])]));
const entries=sources.map((s,i)=>({s,i})).filter(({s})=>s&&typeof s==='object');
const other=entries.filter(({i})=>!used.has(i)||used.get(i)?.has('city-twice'));
const name=(s:Record<string,any>)=>String(s.doc??s.dataset??s.title??s.name??s.url??'Source record');
const validUrl=(url:unknown)=>typeof url==='string'&&/^https:\/\//.test(url)?url:undefined;
---
<Base title="Sources"><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Follow the evidence</p><h1>Sources</h1><p class="lede">The boxes point to public budgets, reports and datasets. A source may describe a budget plan, an estimate or payments for only part of a year. Read each box's label and period before comparing numbers.</p></section><section class="callout"><p>Some source records have no direct web link. We show their document or dataset name rather than invent a URL. Source references also appear on individual box pages. The public repository contains the build instructions and source-file links where available.</p></section><section><h2>Source records in this export</h2><p>The list includes source records cited by detailed boxes, not just the boxes on this page. A record may be cited by many boxes, and the same document can appear in more than one record. Counts here are source records, not boxes.</p>{roots.map(root=>{const subset=entries.filter(({i})=>used.get(i)?.has(root));return <section aria-labelledby={`sources-${root}`}><h3 id={`sources-${root}`}>{titles[root]}: {subset.length.toLocaleString('en-US')} records cited by boxes</h3><ul>{subset.map(({s})=><li>{validUrl(s.url)?<a href={validUrl(s.url)}>{name(s)}</a>:name(s)}{s.period&&<span> ({String(s.period)})</span>}{s.note&&<span> ({String(s.note)})</span>}</li>)}</ul></section>})}<details><summary>Other source records ({other.length.toLocaleString('en-US')})</summary><p>These include the counted-twice memo and source records not grouped above.</p><ol>{other.map(({s,i})=><li value={i+1}>{validUrl(s.url)?<a href={validUrl(s.url)}>{name(s)}</a>:name(s)}{s.period&&` (${String(s.period)})`}</li>)}</ol></details></section></Base>
